The bug is on this line: `const firstVal = value[0]; value.forEach(val => batch.lrem(key, 0, firstVal));`
It's using `firstVal` (the first element of the array) instead of `val` (the current element in the loop). This means if you try to remove ['b', 'd'] from a list, it will try to remove 'b' (the firstVal) multiple times instead of removing each value in the array.

